# --- secrets / local config (NEVER commit) ---
*.env
!*.env.example
bacchus.config.json
bacchus-fyne.config.json
config.json
*.local.json
*.secret
secrets/
*.log

# --- build artifacts ---
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/dist/
/bin/
*-linux
# The device-routing helper, when built into the repo root the way
# deploy/README.md's install steps do (issue #37). Has no extension, so none
# of the patterns above catch it.
/bacchus-netd
*-darwin
*-windows
bacchus-node
bacchus-coordinator
bacchus-turn
bacchus-fyne

# `go build ./cmd/<name>` with no -o writes the binary into the working
# directory under the LAST PATH ELEMENT of the package, which is the command's
# directory name and not the installed name any of the patterns above match:
# ./cmd/node builds `node`, ./cmd/release-sign builds `release-sign`. Every
# command in this repository, so a new one does not have to remember.
/node
/coordinator
/release-sign
/admission-issue
/asn-stage
/bacchus-netd
/capacity-probe
/coldstart-bootstrap
/coldstart-issue
/coldstart-probe
/relaychain-probe

# --- third-party runtime binaries (fetched, NOT vendored) ---
# wintun.dll is proprietary ((c) WireGuard LLC, "licensed, not sold" — see its
# own LICENSE.txt) and must never land in this AGPL repo. It is a Windows runtime
# dependency of clients/fyne, fetched from wintun.net and staged here at
# build/package time. See clients/fyne/README.md ("wintun runtime dependency").
/clients/fyne/wintun/

# --- third-party datasets (fetched, NOT vendored) ---
# The country database the coordinator derives node countries from (issue #136,
# ADR-0042). Bulk data, fetched per host and refreshed out of band, never
# committed. See docs/RUNNING.md ("GeoIP country database").
#
# iptoasn.com's IP-to-Country files are what a coordinator stages (#61). Their
# licence (PDDL) would permit committing them, unlike core/asn/table.tsv.gz which
# is committed for exactly that reason — these are excluded on SIZE and on
# staleness, not on terms: a country table baked into a commit would be wrong
# within weeks and no reader could tell.
ip2country-v4.tsv
ip2country-v6.tsv
ip2country-v*.tsv.gz
#
# deploy/bacchus-geoip-refresh.sh fetches and decompresses under these before renaming
# each family into place, so a coordinator starting mid-refresh cannot read a
# half-written table (issue #85). A completed run leaves none of them behind; a killed
# one can. Excluded for the same two reasons as the files above — they are the same bulk
# data a few seconds earlier, not a different kind of thing.
ip2country-v*.tmp
#
# GeoLite2 remains loadable for a deployment that already staged it. That one is
# a licensed MaxMind dataset under its own terms, which are not ours to
# redistribute under.
/geoip/
GeoLite2-Country-*.csv
GeoLite2-Country-*.mmdb
GeoLite2-Country-CSV_*/

# --- go ---
/vendor/

# --- editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- local scratch notes at the repo root (NEVER commit) ---
# The repo root is where per-checkout notes, task briefs and tooling scratch
# files get dropped, and several such conventions put them in markdown with a
# fixed name. Committing one leaks local working context into a public repo, so
# the root is closed by default and this repo's own documents are allowlisted
# below. This is deliberately a denylist-by-default: it also catches whatever
# the next convention happens to be called, which naming individual files
# cannot. Adding a genuinely new root-level document means adding it here —
# `git add` fails loudly on an ignored path, so it cannot pass unnoticed.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CONVENTIONS.md
!/SECURITY.md
